# Audience And Expectation

<!-- 中文注释：本文件记录本次 PRD 与 Preview 的目标读者、表达风格、用户期待和生成前完整性 Gate。 -->

## Target Readers

| Reader | What They Need To Understand | Required Detail Level |
|---|---|---|
| R&D Team | {{rd_expectation}} | Executable: scope, flows, states, data, acceptance, boundaries |
| Customer / Business Stakeholder | {{customer_expectation}} | Value-readable: problem, value loop, core experience, success signal |
| End User via Preview | {{end_user_preview_expectation}} | Experience-readable: first impression, primary path, CTA, feedback |

## Document Style

- Style: Executable PRD.
- Must be concrete enough for R&D to break down implementation work after technical planning.
- Must be clear enough for customer/business readers to understand the product value and expected user experience.
- Must avoid unconfirmed features, vague slogans, and implementation details outside MVP Definition boundaries.

## Preview Style

- Preview audience: end users.
- Preview must express realistic product experience, not only internal wireframes.
- Preview must make the value proposition, information hierarchy, primary CTA, and key feedback visible.

