## PRD Completeness Gate

| Check | Pass Criteria | Result | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| User and scenario clarity | Target user, core problem, scenario, and current alternative are explicit. | {{gate_user_scenario_result}} | {{gate_user_scenario_notes}} |
| MVP scope discipline | P0 is small enough; P1, Later, and Out of Scope are explicit. | {{gate_scope_result}} | {{gate_scope_notes}} |
| Value loop closure | The user path reaches a clear value moment and has no dead end. | {{gate_value_loop_result}} | {{gate_value_loop_notes}} |
| Page and state coverage | Product surfaces include default, empty, error, and success states. | {{gate_state_result}} | {{gate_state_notes}} |
| Data and visualization clarity | Product data, mock data, and chart axes/units are explicit where needed. | {{gate_data_result}} | {{gate_data_notes}} |
| Acceptance clarity | Product acceptance criteria are observable and judgeable. | {{gate_acceptance_result}} | {{gate_acceptance_notes}} |
| R&D handoff readiness | The PRD is usable for later technical planning and development breakdown. | {{gate_rd_handoff_result}} | {{gate_rd_handoff_notes}} |
| Customer readability | Customer/business readers can understand value, scope, and expected experience. | {{gate_customer_result}} | {{gate_customer_notes}} |
| Preview readiness | The Preview scope can show first-screen value, primary CTA, main path, and feedback. | {{gate_preview_result}} | {{gate_preview_notes}} |

